    <fr:title text="Upstream reusable pieces of Cubical Categorical Logic into agda/cubical">Upstream reusable pieces of Cubical Categorical Logic into <html:code>agda/cubical</html:code></fr:title>
    <fr:taxon>TODO</fr:taxon>
    <fr:meta name="status">pending</fr:meta>
    <fr:meta name="priority">medium</fr:meta>
  </fr:frontmatter>
  <fr:mainmatter>
    <html:p>Identify pieces of <fr:link href="https://github.com/um-catlab/cubical-categorical-logic" type="external">um-catlab/cubical-categorical-logic</fr:link> that are general-purpose enough to belong in the <fr:link href="/cubicalagdalib/" title="The Cubical Agda Library" uri="https://stevenschaefer.net/cubicalagdalib/" display-uri="cubicalagdalib" type="local">Cubical Agda library</fr:link> (<fr:link href="https://github.com/agda/cubical" type="external"><html:code>agda/cubical</html:code></fr:link>), and open upstream PRs for them one at a time.</html:p>
    <fr:tree show-metadata="false">
      <fr:frontmatter>
        <fr:authors>
          <fr:author>
            <fr:link href="/stevenschaefer/" title="Steven Schaefer" uri="https://stevenschaefer.net/stevenschaefer/" display-uri="stevenschaefer" type="local">Steven Schaefer</fr:link>
          </fr:author>
        </fr:authors>
        <fr:date>
          <fr:year>2026</fr:year>
          <fr:month>4</fr:month>
          <fr:day>20</fr:day>
        </fr:date>
        <fr:source-path>/Users/stevenschaefer/forest/trees/sss-009Y.tree</fr:source-path>
        <fr:title text="Why">Why</fr:title>
      </fr:frontmatter>
      <fr:mainmatter>
        <html:p>CCL has accumulated a lot of category-theoretic infrastructure that is not specific to categorical logic — displayed categories, presheaf machinery, universal property boilerplate, standard constructions on functors, etc. Leaving it sequestered in CCL makes it invisible to the wider Cubical community and forces downstream users to depend on the whole of CCL for what should be stdlib utilities. Upstreaming also reduces our long-term maintenance surface.</html:p>
      </fr:mainmatter>
    </fr:tree>
    <fr:tree show-metadata="false">
      <fr:frontmatter>
        <fr:authors>
          <fr:author>
            <fr:link href="/stevenschaefer/" title="Steven Schaefer" uri="https://stevenschaefer.net/stevenschaefer/" display-uri="stevenschaefer" type="local">Steven Schaefer</fr:link>
          </fr:author>
        </fr:authors>
        <fr:date>
          <fr:year>2026</fr:year>
          <fr:month>4</fr:month>
          <fr:day>20</fr:day>
        </fr:date>
        <fr:source-path>/Users/stevenschaefer/forest/trees/sss-009Y.tree</fr:source-path>
        <fr:title text="How">How</fr:title>
      </fr:frontmatter>
      <fr:mainmatter>
        <html:ul><html:li><html:strong>Survey.</html:strong> Walk the CCL module tree and flag files / definitions that are (a) domain-agnostic and (b) not already present in <html:code>Cubical/Categories/</html:code> upstream.</html:li>
<html:li><html:strong>One PR per concept.</html:strong> Follow the same topic-scoped PR discipline Max has asked for on the <fr:link href="/sss-009X/" title="Double Category Theory in Cubical Categorical Logic" uri="https://stevenschaefer.net/sss-009X/" display-uri="sss-009X" type="local">double-category milestone</fr:link>: one upstream PR per definition / construction, not a grab bag.</html:li>
<html:li><html:strong>Keep CCL building.</html:strong> Each landed upstream PR is followed by a CCL-side PR that deletes the local copy and re-imports from stdlib.</html:li>
<html:li><html:strong>Respect stdlib conventions.</html:strong> Naming, file layout, and universe-level handling in <html:code>agda/cubical</html:code> differ from CCL in places — each migration needs a small style pass.</html:li></html:ul>
      </fr:mainmatter>
    </fr:tree>
