            <fr:taxon>Milestone</fr:taxon>
          </fr:frontmatter>
          <fr:mainmatter>
            <html:p>Goal: land the Agda formalization of double categories, double functors, 2-categories, and their main instances in <fr:link href="https://github.com/um-catlab/cubical-categorical-logic" type="external">um-catlab/cubical-categorical-logic</fr:link> as a sequence of <html:em>topic-scoped</html:em> PRs — one PR per concept (definitions, functors, instances, …), reconciled against the thickened-displayed-categories work in <fr:link href="https://github.com/um-catlab/cubical-categorical-logic/pull/253" type="external">PR 253</fr:link>.</html:p>
            <html:p><html:strong>Why a milestone.</html:strong> The material currently lives across a stack of feature branches (<html:code>2-cat</html:code>, <html:code>double-cat</html:code>, <html:code>double-cat-instances</html:code>, <html:code>double-categories</html:code>, <html:code>displayed-double-cat</html:code>, <html:code>thick-displayed-categories</html:code>, plus exploratory branches like <html:code>bicategory-experiment</html:code> and <html:code>investigate-2cat-double-examples</html:code>). Max wants the stack repackaged so each PR addresses a single concept, instead of the current accidental groupings. This milestone tracks that re-slicing without further entangling it with other ongoing work.</html:p>
            <html:p><html:strong>Reconciliation point.</html:strong> The displayed double category construction needs to be expressed against the <html:em>thickened</html:em> displayed categories of <fr:link href="https://github.com/um-catlab/cubical-categorical-logic/pull/253" type="external">PR 253</fr:link> (<html:code>Cubical/Categories/Displayed/Thick/Base.agda</html:code>, plus the <html:code>MappingCylinder</html:code> HIT and the freely-adjoined-identity construction). Until 253 lands, the <html:code>displayed-double-cat</html:code> branch's WIP instance (<html:code>Cubical/Categories/Double/Instances/Displayed.agda</html:code>, currently with holes) is the natural client and stress test.</html:p>
            <html:p><html:strong>Sections.</html:strong> Each section below is its own tree; the milestone tracks them via transclusion. Work items (individual PRs) are separate TODO trees tagged <html:code>subtask-of-sss-009X</html:code> plus the relevant topic tag, surfaced through the section's Datalog query.</html:p>
